Type Guards: Leverage TypeScript’s type guards to narrow types whenever possible.
Unit Testing: Write tests for various valid and invalid inputs to ensure your validation logic behaves as expected.
Sanitization: In addition to validation, consider sanitizing inputs to remove any unexpected or harmful data.
