Validating tool arguments is an essential aspect of building robust and secure agent systems. By implementing stringent validation routines, your system can avoid unexpected errors and ensure that only correct, safe inputs are processed by the agent’s tools. The provided TypeScript example serves as a starting point for integrating argument validation in a real-world tool-calling scenario.

