8. Common Mistakes
Ignoring Asynchronous Nature:
Developers may forget to await the asynchronous operation or the timeout, leading to premature resolution.

Improper Delay Calculation:
Miscalculating the exponential delay formula or omitting jitter can lead to synchronized retry storms in distributed scenarios.

Not Handling Maximum Attempt Boundaries:
Failing to break out of the loop once the maximum number of attempts is reached results in an infinite loop or unhandled exceptions.

Overcomplicating Cancellation:
Avoid adding cancellation tokens unless required; ensure that the retry logic cleanly rejects after the final attempt.

Lack of Logging/Monitoring:
